 ### Review fixes (2026-11-12)
 
-- Room id compatibility: the real 001 database seeds `common-room`, so the id is kept as-is; `server/index.mjs` now uses one `ROOM_ID` constant instead of `room-main`. The display name stays `共同房间`.
+- Room id compatibility: the real 001 database seeds `common-room`, so the id is kept as-is; `server/index.mjs` now uses one `ROOM_ID` constant instead of the former hard-coded id. The display name stays `共同房间`.
 - Migration test now uses the real `common-room` seed and asserts that bootstrap finds the old message after `001 → 002` (and that seeding does not add a second room).
 - `runs.reply_message_id` added in `002_p01`; the success path stores the reply message id.
 
+### P0.1.1 migration-test hardening (2026-11-12)
+
+- Rebuilt the old database from the real `001_initial.sql` (`CURRENT_TIMESTAMP` format, two messages, one event), migrated it, then started `createApp` and asserted `/api/bootstrap` returns the original room name and both messages in order.
+- Added FK checks after migration: `PRAGMA foreign_keys` must be `1`, invalid `messages.room_id`, `messages.reply_to_id`, and `runs.trigger_message_id` inserts must throw, and `PRAGMA foreign_key_check` must stay empty.
+- Success path now asserts `run.trigger_message_id = human message`, `run.reply_message_id = reply message`, and `reply.reply_to_id = human message`; failure path asserts `reply_message_id IS NULL`.
+- Temp directories are removed with `maxRetries: 3, retryDelay: 50` to tolerate Windows WAL handle release.
+
 ### Verification
 
-- `npm test`: 9 tests, 0 failures. Covers bootstrap, ISO round-trip, malformed URL survival, cross-site/token/content-type rejection, runtime failure preservation, second message during a delayed runtime, FakeRuntime stream modes, member CHECK/foreign keys, and `001 → 002` data migration.
+- `npm test`: 10 tests, 0 failures. Covers bootstrap, ISO round-trip, malformed URL survival, cross-site/token/content-type rejection, runtime failure preservation, second message during a delayed runtime, FakeRuntime stream modes, member CHECK/foreign keys, fresh-database FK enforcement, and a real `001 → 002` migration read through `/api/bootstrap`.
 - `npm run build`: passed (`tsc --noEmit` + Vite production build).
 - `npm start` requires a local browser Origin or the printed token; the browser UI is unchanged apart from UTC-safe time rendering and a refresh after a 502.
